{"tag":"AN0F","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2610.07876","version":"1","local":"teo-1","file":"","label":"main","number":"0.1","order":1,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{main}\nThere exists a universal constant $L$ such that for any subgaussian random vector $X$ in $\\mathbb{R}^N$ and any convex function $\\varphi$ with $\\mathsf{E}\\varphi(G)\u003c\\infty$, we have\n$$\\mathsf{E}\\varphi(X/L)\\leq \\mathsf{E} \\varphi(G).$$","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"teo","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"teo","number_from":"render","name":"Subgaussian convex-order comparison","labels":["main"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"cited","origin":"cited","span":{"file":"subgaussian_comparison.tex","from":121,"to":124},"hash":"sha256:fcc45003db4e23825074fdb1216a3efe9b228e50499c35410536e8d56dc7ab7e","minhash":"","census":"2610.07876v1#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.29"}
{"tag":"3WQX","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2610.07876","version":"1","local":"lem-1","file":"","label":"lemma","number":"0.2","order":2,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{lemma}\nThere exists a universal constant $L$ with the following property.  Consider a  subgaussian random vector $X$ in $\\mathbb{R}^N$, standard Gaussian vector $G$ in $\\mathbb{R}^N$ and a convex set $C$ in $\\mathbb{R}^N$ with $\\mathsf{P}(G\\in C)\\geq 7/8$. Then $\\mathsf{P}(X\\in LC)\\geq 1/2$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"teo","number_from":"render","labels":["lemma"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"subgaussian_comparison.tex","from":145,"to":147},"hash":"sha256:e870f626d49b0ff63ad8578ed022bf4c4b2d30cb1faeb893124158e2a6c42a2e","minhash":"","census":"2610.07876v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.29"}
